# stark_input options, shown in the single STARK menu: main/Kconfig.projbuild
# sources this file (ARCHITECTURE.md §9). ESP-IDF does not pick up a
# `Kconfig.stark` on its own, so the menu is assembled in one place.

config STARK_INPUT_POLL_MS
    int "Key sampling period (ms)"
    default 5
    help
        Period of the esp_timer that samples the six key GPIOs and runs
        the debounce/repeat core (components/stark_input). The debounce,
        long-press and repeat timings are separate and do not depend on
        this. ARCHITECTURE.md §6.6, §9.

config STARK_INPUT_REPEAT_DELAY_MS
    int "Key repeat delay (ms)"
    range 150 1000
    default 400
    help
        How long UP/DOWN/LEFT/RIGHT must be held before they start to
        repeat. Tuned on hardware at the V1 prototype ("repeat timing feels
        right", TESTING.md §5); the same value in simulation and on the
        board (ADR-0010). Runtime adjustment is V0.2's settings.

config STARK_INPUT_REPEAT_INTERVAL_MS
    int "Key repeat interval (ms)"
    range 40 500
    default 120
    help
        Time between two repeats while a direction key stays held.
